    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57819": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher for Dr. Zhu - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Postdoctoral Researcher for Dr. Zhu - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Postdoctoral Researcher for Dr. Zhu - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application and attach the required documents. Required documents include a detailed cover letter, current resume, and a list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by the posting close date. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Postdoctoral Researcher for Dr. Zhu - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application and attach the required documents. Required documents include a detailed cover letter, current resume, and a list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by the posting close date. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016533T Job Description Summary Department Summary About the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine: Mission: We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio. Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community commits itself to: providing a clinically integrated, learning-centered, osteopathic medical education continuum for students, interns, residents and primary care associates; embracing public service; and improving the health and well-being of underserved populations. Vision: A healthier Ohio, empowered by compassionate osteopathic physicians. With our graduates and partners, we advance care and knowledge to improve the health of our communities. Our culture is built upon resiliency, courage and compassion. Our physicians humanize each patient encounter, bridging the gap between therapeutics, medical technologies, health systems, care delivery and disparity. Essential Values: These fundamental principles form the foundation of the culture at our college: wholeness and balance within each person; integrity; community of mutual respect; acceptance of others; pursuit of excellence; a climate of scholarship; and commitment to service, generosity and compassion. Our Campuses https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses Why Choose Ohio University? https://www.ohio.edu/hr/jobs/working-ohio https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits About the Department of Biomedical Sciences https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/departments/biomedical Position Summary: The Postdoctoral Researcher in Dr. Shouan Zhu’s osteoarthritis research laboratory leads research projects investigating the molecular and metabolic mechanisms underlying osteoarthritis and musculoskeletal aging. The laboratory focuses on understanding how aging, obesity, metabolic dysfunction, and joint injury contribute to cartilage degeneration, with particular interests in lipid and energy metabolism, post-translational modifications, inflammatory signaling, and the growth hormone/ IGF -1 pathway. The Postdoctoral Researcher will use complementary in vitro and in vivo approaches, including molecular and cell biology, mouse models, histology, metabolic studies, and multi-omics analyses. This position will work closely with the Principal Investigator (PI) on projects with strong potential for first-author publications, conference presentations, and development toward an independent research career. This is a one-year term position with the possibility of extension. Position Responsibilities: Plan, design, and conduct original research investigating mechanisms of osteoarthritis, cartilage degeneration, and musculoskeletal aging, with particular emphasis on metabolic and inflammatory pathways associated with aging, obesity, and joint injury. Perform experiments using cellular and animal models and techniques that may include primary cell and tissue culture, molecular biology, RT-qPCR, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, immunofluorescence, histology, metabolic assays, and advanced imaging. Conduct and assist with in vivo mouse studies involving genetic, aging, obesity, and injury-associated models of osteoarthritis, including animal monitoring, experimental interventions, tissue collection, processing, histological evaluation, and phenotypic analyses. Studies may incorporate transcriptomics, single-cell RNA sequencing, proteomics, metabolomics, lipidomics, and other multi-omics approaches. Maintain accurate experimental records, perform quantitative and statistical analyses, interpret experimental findings, troubleshoot technical problems, and work with the PI to develop new hypotheses and research directions. Prepare manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals under the guidance of the PI. Assist with literature reviews, grant applications, progress reports, and other scientific documents. Present research findings at laboratory and departmental meetings and at national and international scientific conferences. Work collaboratively with faculty, research staff, graduate students, medical students, and undergraduate researchers. Assist with training and mentoring students in experimental techniques, data analysis, and scientific communication. Contribute to interdisciplinary collaborations in musculoskeletal biology, aging, metabolism, and related research areas and help maintain a rigorous and collegial research environment. Position Profile Working under the guidance of a faculty member or principal investigator, conducts advanced, independent and collaborative research, contributes to research design, execution, analysis, and publication, and builds specialized expertise in field of study. Serves as a leader on research projects and mentors students. Presents at conferences and seminars, prepares manuscripts for peer-reviewed publications, and contributes to grant proposals as required. Level Summary Provides professional expertise to the University community. Serves as a resource and guide to others in the department and/or university. Works on both strategic and operational challenges, addressing problems that require advanced knowledge and experience. Often takes on leadership roles in projects or initiatives. Supervisory Responsibilities None; may assist with training student employees. Fiscal Responsibilities No budgetary responsibility. May be responsible for validating transactions. Problem Solving Handles a variety of problems with some independence. Independence of Action Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with peers and follows guidance from supervisor. Shares knowledge with team members. Physical Requirements This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. The position is based in a standard research wet-lab and office environment and may occasionally require travel to attend meetings and programs. The position requires frequent use of vision and hearing and occasional prolonged standing and walking at laboratory benches. The role may also involve frequent exposure to biohazardous materials, chemical hazards, and tissue-processing reagents commonly encountered in biomedical research. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a related field. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree in Biomedical Engineering, Biological Sciences, Molecular and Cellular Biology, Biochemistry, Physiology, Immunology, Metabolism, Musculoskeletal Biology, or a closely related field. ABD candidates may be considered provided the degree will be conferred within six months of hire. Strong research background in one or more areas relevant to the laboratory, including metabolism, obesity, immunometabolism, lipid biology, macrophage/inflammatory biology, epigenetics, aging, or musculoskeletal biology. Substantial hands-on experience with molecular and cellular biology techniques such as cell culture, RNA and protein analysis, RT-qPCR, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, immunofluorescence, and related approaches. Experience with animal models, tissue collection, histology, or metabolic-disease models Experience with transcriptomic, single-cell, proteomic, metabolomic, lipidomic, or other omics approaches. Experience with R, Python, bioinformatics, or quantitative data analysis. Experience in osteoarthritis, cartilage biology, metabolic disease, immunometabolism, or related areas. Strong scientific writing and communication skills, with evidence of productivity through peer-reviewed publications, manuscripts, or conference presentations. Demonstrated self-motivation, creativity, problem-solving ability, attention to experimental rigor, and ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Department HCOM - Biomedical Sciences Pay Rate Pay is commensurate with the candidate’s education and experience in relation to the minimum qualifications for the position. Pay is accompanied by Ohio University’s generous benefits package, which includes: Free tuition for employees and dependents Comprehensive insurance coverage, including health, prescription, vision, dental, orthodontia, and life insurance An excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution Wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a robust employee assistance program Paid parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more Additional information is available at: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/ Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade RES 01 Pay Range $43,888.00+ FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Research Special at-will appointment Employment Type full-time term Job Family Research Administration Job Sub Family Postdoc Job Level POSTDOC Job Open Date 10/05/2026 Posting End Date 11/01/2026 Planning Unit Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Work Schedule Monday through Friday 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Some after hours and weekend work may be required to complete experimental protocols and biological sample processing. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 Expected duration of assignment one-year term Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Jordyn Boyer, jboyer@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57211": {
      "title": "Instructor, Geography (non-tenure track, part-time) POOL POSTING",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Instructor, Geography (non-tenure track, part-time) POOL POSTING Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Instructor, Geography (non-tenure track, part-time) POOL POSTING Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We are accepting resumes/CVs for openings in the Department of Geography for academic year 2026-2027. Applications will be considered to fill a part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions at the Athens campus. Applications will be accepted through July 15, 2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue as needs arise throughout the year. Please complete the online application and upload a current CV, letter of interest, and a list of three professional references. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Instructor, Geography (non-tenure track, part-time) POOL POSTING Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants We are accepting resumes/CVs for openings in the Department of Geography for academic year 2026-2027. Applications will be considered to fill a part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions at the Athens campus. Applications will be accepted through July 15, 2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue as needs arise throughout the year. Please complete the online application and upload a current CV, letter of interest, and a list of three professional references. This position is eligible for the following benefits: sick leave and retirement. Posting Number 20163199F Job Description Applications for the positions will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions for the Department of Geography. The selected candidates may teach a large introduction level class or combined undergraduate and graduate courses. Duties include student assessment and may include teaching a lab. Minimum Qualifications Candidates must have a Masters degree in Geography or related field and relevant teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with a PhD in Geography and have an established record of teaching. Department Geography Pay Rate Pay is set according to college approved rates. Please visit A&S Summer and Overload Course Policy | Ohio University for more information. Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. User Selection Field Job Open Date 07/16/2026 Posting Close Date 07/15/2027 Employment Type Temporary (for group 3 ONLY) Job Category Instructor Months variable month Planning Unit College of Arts & Sciences Work Schedule Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Joey Pierce, Employment Coordinator, piercej@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required