    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57893": {
      "title": "Outdoor Pursuit Assistant",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Outdoor Pursuit Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Outdoor Pursuit Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, complete the online application and upload the following documents: Required: Resume Cover Letter document qualifications for the position Other-CPR/First Aid Certification Questions should be directed to Hans Rudolph, Assistant Director of Outdoor Recreation and Education, rudolphh@ohio.edu Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Outdoor Pursuit Assistant Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, complete the online application and upload the following documents: Required: Resume Cover Letter document qualifications for the position Other- CPR /First Aid Certification Questions should be directed to Hans Rudolph, Assistant Director of Outdoor Recreation and Education, rudolphh@ohio.edu Posting Number 20161778STD Department Summary This position requires flexibility, professionalism, and a commitment to being a member of the Outdoor Pursuits team. Outdoor Pursuits employees are expected to work in all four of the program areas: Climbing Wall, Challenge Course, Rental Center, Trips/Clinics. Outdoor Pursuits employees have a commitment to upholding the mission, vision, and values of Ohio University Recreation. This is Outdoor Pursuits’ entry-level position. All staff are hired to Outdoor Pursuits as an OPA . Staff work in the OPA role when working as a secondary staff member at the climbing wall or when attending any generalized all-staff training. While at the climbing wall and service desk, Outdoor Pursuits Assistants are responsible for providing a high quality customer service experience for all patrons of the climbing wall and service desk, maintaining a safe environment through routine safety checks of equipment, constant monitoring of patrons’ rigging and belay technique, providing a clean and organized program and service area, entering information into the participant database, and assisting patrons to better ensure a safe and fun climbing experience. Working in the rental center may include knowledge of reservations, rentals, returns, and resale, monitoring inventory, and cleaning, repairing, and restocking of rental equipment. Challenge Course Facilitators are responsible for everything related to challenge program events including developing the activity schedule, setting the course, and ensuring that the days’ events run smoothly and safely. Facilitators blend a combination of interpersonal skills, technical skills, and a desire to work with people to provide meaningful educational experiences to challenge program participants. Trip Leaders are responsible for leading eligible participants through adventure recreation activities and instructing outdoor clinics. They must participate in outdoor adventure trip and clinic planning and implementation while considering participant and group safety, experience, and interests. They ensure that all planning and implementation of trips are in accordance with Outdoor Pursuits policies and procedures. Responsibilities: Must display dependability, motivation, and adaptability Know and enforce all policies and procedures Maintain a safe and clean environment for both staff and participants Review and complete all necessary paperwork, and any paperwork created during shift Participation and completion of all in-service training sessions and mandatory meetings Effectively communicate with patrons, fellow staff, supervisors, Graduate Assistants, and Assistant Director of Outdoor Pursuits Regularly check and respond to work-related emails Respond to patrons’ inquiries or concerns and refer them to Supervisor or Management Staff when needed Completion of additional duties as assigned by the Supervisor and Management Staff Area Specific Responsibilities: (If you are unsure about some of the following responsibilities, additional training will be provided. We ask that you have a willingness to learn these skills and responsibilities.) Climbing Wall: Thorough knowledge of PBUS belay technique, GriGri 2 and ATC set up, and ability to instruct proper use of participant harnesses Professional yet friendly interactions with all wall patrons Constant monitoring of patrons belay technique and overall safety Attend climbing wall related meetings and trainings Service Desk: Fill out, file, and enter into the computer all paperwork including waivers, belay certifications, and rental agreements Maintain a safe environment for participants at Climbing Wall Track patron use of the wall and other programs in DSE Assist patrons with registering for Outdoor Pursuits programs Rental Center: Knowledge of outdoor equipment and related activities Ability to thoroughly clean and assess needed repair of equipment Ability to maintain a clean and organized work space Challenge Program: Develop and facilitate learning-centered challenge program experiences Maintain a safe environment for both staff and participants Complete all tasks associated with opening and closing the Outdoor Pursuits Challenge Course Review and complete all necessary paperwork, e.g. daily checklists, incident reports, feedback forms Attend Challenge Program related meetings and trainings Trips & Clinics: Oversee safety and welfare of outdoor adventure trip participants (often in remote settings) Assist with all trip logistics and itinerary planning Select activities based on participants’ skill level Attend trip leader trainings and meetings Complete trip evaluation and review sessions with Student Supervisor and Graduate Assistant as needed Complete trip related paperwork and equipment check out Safely operate all university owned vehicles Knowledge and Skills: A commitment to upholding positive, intentional, and consistent customer service Strong accountability to your responsibilities Dependable and self-motivated Ability to educate patrons about Outdoor Pursuits and its offerings in a welcoming and positive manner Job Profile Leads recreational classes or activities centering on fitness, sports, or wellness programs for students. May include creating lesson plans, developing personal training plans, maintaining safety standards, and fostering a positive environment. Certification may be required to lead certain programs. Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. Roles are entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University, Hocking College, another post-secondary education institution, or a secondary school during the current semester, immediate previous semester, or immediate upcoming semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Preferred Qualifications First Aid / Adult CPR / AED Belay trained through Ohio University Outdoor Pursuits Successful completion of Ohio University Outdoor Pursuits trainings Working Condition/Physical Demands: This role involves occasional work on computers but is primarily active work. Employees in this position should expect to work indoors and outdoors in all weather conditions. Department Outdoor Pursuits Pay Rate $12.30/hour FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 10/05/2026 Posting End Date 11/02/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Vice President for Student Life Work Schedule We will work with you and your academic classes to make your schedule Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Hans Rudolph, rudolphh@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Student Recreation Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Other (See Special Instructions to Applicants for Details) Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
