mary Join University Human Resources as a student assistant and gain hands-on experience supporting HR projects and initiatives. The student assistant will work with HR team members to help coordinate projects, track progress and deadlines, organize information, and assist with a variety of administrative and project-based tasks. Federal Work Study eligibility is required. An interview is required for this position. Job Profile Level Summary Supervisory Responsibilities: Fiscal Responsibilities: Problem Solving: Independence of Action: Communication and Collaboration: Minimum Qualifications Federal Work Study Award Preferred Qualifications Working Condition/Physical Demands: Office position. Department University Human Resources Pay Rate FLSA Status Posting Open Date 10/15/2026 Posting End Date 12/31/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Office of the President Work Schedule Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level Job Family Job Sub Family Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Requir