    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57755": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Ohio University has launched a search for an Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries, with the goal of having the position filled before the 2026–27 spring semester begins. Applications should include, as separate documents, a CV or resume, a letter of interest, and a list of professional references with current contact information, including email addresses. The letter of interest should highlight the candidate’s qualifications, relevant experience, leadership accomplishments, and demonstrated success in areas that align with the responsibilities and priorities of the position as outlined in the Leadership Profile here: Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries Search | Ohio University The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by the posting end date. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Ohio University has launched a search for an Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries, with the goal of having the position filled before the 2026–27 spring semester begins. Applications should include, as separate documents, a CV or resume, a letter of interest, and a list of professional references with current contact information, including email addresses. The letter of interest should highlight the candidate’s qualifications, relevant experience, leadership accomplishments, and demonstrated success in areas that align with the responsibilities and priorities of the position as outlined in the Leadership Profile here: Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries Search | Ohio University The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by the posting end date. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016520T Job Description Summary Department Summary Ohio University invites applications and nominations for the position of Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries within the Division of Student Life. Reporting to the Interim Vice President for Student Life, the Associate Vice President provides strategic leadership for an auxiliary portfolio that includes Culinary Services and Housing and Residence Life. Key Responsibilities: This senior leader will guide complex, self-supporting operations that play an essential role in the daily experience of students, employees, campus visitors, and community members. The Associate Vice President will establish and communicate departmental goals, implement effective business systems and practices, cultivate an entrepreneurial and customer-focused environment, and promote a culture centered on student success, safety, service, accountability, and continuous improvement. The position also provides strategic direction for long-range capital planning, preventive maintenance, facilities renewal and renovation, security, program development, and evolving product and service offerings. Working closely with professional leadership staff and university partners, the Associate Vice President will identify new business opportunities, establish appropriate service levels, address compliance matters in collaboration with campus partners, and ensure continuity of operations. Leadership Portfolio: The Associate Vice President provides leadership and directional oversight for the following areas: Culinary Services Culinary Services is a $57 million dining, catering, retail, and culinary production enterprise serving Ohio University. The operation includes dining commons, food courts, retail markets, coffee shops, catering venues, a full-service restaurant, food trucks, and an extensive culinary production and distribution network. With more than 70 administrative employees, 188 bargaining-unit staff, and approximately 1,500 student employees, the department requires strategic leadership across financial management, operations, retail, catering, logistics, workforce development, customer experience, and business growth initiatives. Housing and Residence Life Housing and Residence Life oversees a $59 million housing and residential education enterprise that supports approximately 8,000 students across 36 residence halls. The department is among the university’s largest and most complex operations, employing more than 400 full-time, part-time, graduate, and student staff members. The complete Leadership Profile can be reviewed here: Associate Vice President for Auxiliaries Search | Ohio University Position Profile Responsible for auxiliary functions within Student Affairs, including Housing, Culinary, and Retail operations. Provides strategic direction to enhance operational efficiency, drive revenue growth, and promote financial sustainability. Level Summary Responsible for the strategic direction and oversight of complex functional areas or multiple departments. Formulates policies, strategies, and systems that enhance the University’s position in the competitive marketplace. Leads large, complex teams, possibly managing multiple layers of managers. Contributes to shaping the long-term strategic vision of the University, ensuring alignment with overarching goals. Supervisory Responsibilities Manages entire business units or divisions. Has authority to hire, transfer, suspend, promote, manage performance, discharge, assign duties, reward, and discipline employees. Fiscal Responsibilities Oversees multi-million dollar budget. Problem Solving Solves highly complex, University-wide problems with long-term consequences. Independence of Action Full autonomy in decision-making, accountable for business outcomes. Communication and Collaboration Leads communication with senior leaders, partners, and internal/external stakeholders. Responsible for successful implementation of organizational goals. Physical Requirements Work is primarily performed in an office and meeting environment. The position will require travel to meetings and events. Minimum Qualifications A master’s degree in business administration, higher education administration, hospitality management, finance, public administration, facilities management, or a related field. 10+ years of progressively responsible leadership experience in auxiliary services, higher education administration, hospitality, housing, dining, retail, conference services, facilities, or another comparably complex operational environment. A bachelor’s degree and an additional two years of progressively responsible leadership experience beyond the experience requirement listed above may also be considered. Demonstrated experience managing significant budgets, revenue-producing operations, and multidisciplinary teams. Experience leading strategic planning, operational improvement, financial stewardship, and organizational change. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with a broad range of internal and external stakeholders. Strong communication, decision-making, and problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications An advanced degree in a relevant field. Senior-level leadership experience within higher education or a similarly complex, mission-driven organization. Experience overseeing multiple auxiliary or enterprise operations. Experience with capital planning, facilities renewal, construction, renovation, or preventive maintenance. Experience working in a collective-bargaining environment. Demonstrated success developing new programs, services, partnerships, or revenue opportunities. Experience using data, benchmarking, and performance measures to support decision-making and continuous improvement. Familiarity with legal, compliance, safety, and risk-management considerations associated with large-scale auxiliary operations. Department VP For Student Life Pay Rate Competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Employees enjoy a generous benefits package https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade EXEC Pay Range Executive FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Student Affairs Job Sub Family Student Affairs Strategy Job Level EXEC Job Open Date 09/25/2026 Posting End Date 11/01/2026 Planning Unit Vice President for Student Life Work Schedule Standard administrative work schedule, with flexibility required for evening and weekend meetings, events, and other university responsibilities. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 + Expected duration of assignment on-going Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Megan Vogel, vogelm@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? www. ohiouniversityjobs.com www.higheredjobs.com www.ohiomeansjobs.com The Athens Messenger The Chronicle of Higher Education Ohio University employee OHIO Jobs Line (phone) Employment Agency Posted Announcement Professional association Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, etc) OTHER Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
