    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57862": {
      "title": "LINKS Peer Mentor",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | LINKS Peer Mentor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC LINKS Peer Mentor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. For consideration for this position students are required to complete the application found here: LINKS Peer Mentor Application Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title LINKS Peer Mentor Special Instructions to Applicants For consideration for this position students are required to complete the application found here: LINKS Peer Mentor Application Posting Number 20161782STD Department Summary Housed within Signature Academic Experiences, the LINKS program is a first-year student support program that helps students navigate their transition to Ohio University and develop meaningful connections with peers, campus resources, academic interests, and potential career pathways. LINKS emphasizes well-being, campus engagement, personal development, academic and professional development, and a sense of belonging within the Bobcat community. Every LINKS student is paired with a returning-student peer mentor who provides individualized peer support and maintains regular contact throughout the academic year. The LINKS Peer Mentor position contributes to this mission by serving as a positive peer role model and a supportive point of connection for first-year students. Peer Mentors help students navigate their transition to college, identify and connect with appropriate campus resources, explore academic and career interests, participate in program activities, and build meaningful connections within the OHIO community. Peer Mentors work under the supervision of the LINKS Assistant Director and collaborate with the LINKS team to support student engagement and success. Job Profile Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Offers academic and/or well-being support to fellow students, helping them navigate academic, social, or personal challenges. Responsibilities may include providing peer counseling, resources, and referrals to other campus services. Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. Roles are entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University, Hocking College, another post-secondary education institution, or a secondary school during the current semester, immediate previous semester, or immediate upcoming semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Preferred Qualifications Ability to balance academic responsibilities with employment and leadership commitments. Previous LINKS mentee, experience as a peer mentor, leadership, student organization, resident assistant, orientation, student employment, or other student-support role. Working Condition/Physical Demands: Work may include individual or group contact with assigned LINKS students, participation in required team meetings or trainings, program activities, student outreach, resource navigation, and other approved mentoring responsibilities. Department Signature Academic Experiences Pay Rate $11.40/ hour FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 10/09/2026 Posting End Date 10/23/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Office of the Provost Work Schedule This position is limited to a maximum of 5 hours per week during the academic year. This position provides a flexible student employment opportunity that complements, rather than interferes with, the Peer Mentor’s academic responsibilities. work hours are flexible and determined by mentor/mentee availability. Includes some individual and group contact with assigned LINKS students. Participation in required team meetings, trainings, program activities, student outreach, resource navigation, and other approved mentoring responsibilities. Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Crystal Asimenu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Peer Support Specialist Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
