    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57927": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Student Affairs, Athens Campus - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Associate Director, Student Affairs, Athens Campus - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Associate Director, Student Affairs, Athens Campus - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application and attach the required documents. Required documents include a detailed cover letter, current resume, and a list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by the posting close date. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Associate Director, Student Affairs, Athens Campus - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application and attach the required documents. Required documents include a detailed cover letter, current resume, and a list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by the posting close date. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016552T Job Description Summary Department Summary About the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine: Mission: We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio. Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community commits itself to: providing a clinically integrated, learning-centered, osteopathic medical education continuum for students, interns, residents and primary care associates; embracing public service; and improving the health and well-being of underserved populations. Vision: A healthier Ohio, empowered by compassionate osteopathic physicians. With our graduates and partners, we advance care and knowledge to improve the health of our communities. Our culture is built upon resiliency, courage and compassion. Our physicians humanize each patient encounter, bridging the gap between therapeutics, medical technologies, health systems, care delivery and disparity. Essential Values: These fundamental principles form the foundation of the culture at our college: wholeness and balance within each person; integrity; community of mutual respect; acceptance of others; pursuit of excellence; a climate of scholarship; and commitment to service, generosity and compassion. Our Campuses: https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses Why Choose Ohio University? https://www.ohio.edu/hr/jobs/working-ohio https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits About the Office of Student Affairs https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/offices/student-affairs Department Summary: The Associate Director, Student Affairs oversees and guides the processes and programs that enhance the medical student experience and Heritage College multi-campus success by serving as an advisor, developer, and coordinator for student life activities and student organization events involving leadership, professionalism, research, and career development. The position also advises the student government association, class officers, and student organizations. Position provides longitudinal health and wellness support during Years 1-4 of the medical school program in alignment with the Heritage College prioritization of the student experience. The position requires the use of crisis management techniques as students may seek immediate support for perceived/actual academic, personal, and professional challenges. Department Responsibilities: Student Support Direct Student Government and lead Student Organization efforts for the Heritage College campus site. Responsible for leading and developing the student government, class cohorts, and club/organization executive officers representing the Heritage College and medical school program. This role involves collaborating with college/university partners and guiding student leaders in adhering to objectives, planning timelines, and ensuring impactful programming outcomes for each initiative and project. Conduct scheduled and impromptu one-on-one meetings related to general health and wellness check-ins, student development, and leadership coaching. Advise and speak with students regarding issues of professionalism, campus expectations, behaviors, and approaches to situations involving student peers, staff, faculty, physicians/preceptors, and external site partners. Develop, maintain, and oversee the implementation of student leadership training, including program planning, college event process scheduling, facilitation, and post event/activity assessment. Train, establish objectives, and educate Heritage faculty club/organization advisors in best practices of mentoring and advising. Serve as campus liaison in identifying specific approaches and applicable student resources related to student success and wellbeing. Respond, support, and direct students experiencing personal or professional challenges or distress. Advise medical students in relation to interpersonal conduct and impairments. Refer and advise students to appropriate resources and support services Events and Operations Guide the vision, strategy, planning, organization, and implementation of Signature Student Affairs Heritage College events within a multi-campus environment. This may include but is not limited to orientation, commencement, wellness events, community engagement, and other student programming. Collaborate with Student Affairs and Academic Affairs to design and deliver a seamless, coordinated new-student orientation and onboarding experience across campuses, with responsibility for budgeting, programming, resource scheduling, and staffing. Advance innovative activities to enhance the campus culture and educational experience. Work with local vendors, local area primary and secondary schools, partnering physicians and medical/medical education professionals, other professional organizations, and various Ohio University departments as needed on programming, events, and outreach initiatives. Collaborate with internal/external constituents and senior leadership to lead key initiatives and develop programming for students related to the health and wellness enterprises at the college as it aligns with the Heritage College strategy. Regularly serves as a technical leader, expert, and/or program manager for challenging and unique functions and programs that have direct and important department level impact including but not limited to: Heritage College Orientation, Student Class Officer / Government Elections, Commencement, Heritage Gala / Formal Evening celebration for medical students Assess and revise Heritage College curricular and student event schedule in a multi-department team-based format; identify resource and event support needed. Serve as a site-based approver and authority on proposed programs/initiatives via college events scheduling process for all Heritage campuses. Develop processes and procedures for governing student life and the use of the facilities and resources pertinent to campus location Budget and Account Management Budget management responsibilities may include but are not limited to HCOM Commencement budget, the HCOM Student Orientation Week Budget, Wellness Committee Budget. and the Student Mass Funding Request Budget. Coordinate with the Bursar, OHIO Finance, and Heritage College finance/budget teams on Student Organization accounts to develop/refine procedures, and account development. Develop budget forecasts for expenditures and identify other factors influencing budgets as requested/reviewed by the Senior Director of Student Affairs Oversee campus student funding request process, eligibility determination, and budget management with the Heritage College designated student mass funding process supporting professional travel and showcasing of medical student research efforts. Oversight of Heritage College club/organization registration (totaling over 100) and associated budget accounts to ensure each entity remains in compliance with national and local guidelines, with funds spent appropriately. Contribute to expense monitoring and budget management responsibilities for site specific Student Affairs operational accounts. Coordinate with University Bursar, OHIO Finance, and Heritage College finance/budget teams on student organization account development and current procedures. Aids in site management of expense processing and cash handling (deposits) for all student organization accounts. Administration Develop new or revised departmental procedures, in collaboration with Heritage College Student Affairs leadership, based on assessment of college and student needs. Assist in the production of specific elements of the Medical Student Performance Evaluation ( MSPE ) for prescribed group of students. Identify, develop, and communicate student performance information that best represents the individual as it relates to club and organizational involvement, noteworthy characteristics, and other pertinent information. Collaborate with department to update the Student Resource Manual to reflect site policies and information. Assess and reconfigure programs and processes as necessary to achieve excellence in service to medical students and ensure processes and practices are in compliance with required policies, procedures, and laws. Ensure OHIO conduct and safety compliance by serving as a trained Campus Security Authority ( CSA ) in association with annual Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). Additionally maintain up-to-date training on OHIO Minors on Campus procedures and protocols when hosting applicable events and populations. Represent Student Affairs on College and University committees as needed. May supervise administrative professionals, graduate students, and/or student employees as available. Position Profile Supports the student experience outside the classroom by developing and implementing programs that promote student integration, well-being, and success. Develops and implements student non-academic programs, services, and activities, including residential life, social events, public service, student conduct, leadership development, student organization advising, and other areas. Level Summary Manages and resolves complex and ambiguous issues. Works on both strategic and operational challenges, addressing problems that require advanced knowledge and experience. Often takes on leadership roles in projects or initiatives. Supervisory Responsibilities Provides mentorship and guidance to team. Infrequently has a limited number of direct reports. Fiscal Responsibilities May have budgetary responsibility for small-scale projects or initiatives. Problem Solving Solves complex problems, often with limited guidance. Independence of Action Works independently; seeks guidance for unusual situations. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with team members and external departments. May represent the team in meetings with internal and external stakeholders. Physical Requirements This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Occasionally, the job may require travel to attend meetings and programs. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Bachelor’s degree in a related field and 5 or more years of related professional experience, or equivalent education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in student Personnel, Communications, or Higher Education Administration Master’s degree Experience advising in an academic setting Department HCOM - Student Affairs Pay Rate The approved hiring range for this position is $44,592 to $59,085 . Offers outside of this range require additional approvals. The final offer will be commensurate with the candidate’s education and experience in relation to the minimum qualifications for the position. Pay is accompanied by Ohio University’s generous benefits package, which includes: Free tuition for employees and dependents Comprehensive insurance coverage, including health, prescription, vision, dental, orthodontia, and life insurance An excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution Wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a robust employee assistance program Paid parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more Additional information is available at: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/ Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 16 Pay Range $44,592.00-$74,196.00 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Student Affairs Job Sub Family Student Life & Development Job Level IC3 Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Posting End Date 11/08/2026 Planning Unit Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Work Schedule Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. Some after hours, weekend, and holiday work may be required. Flexplace and flextime arrangements may be available for this position. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 Expected duration of assignment on-going Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Jordyn Boyer, jboyer@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
