    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57575": {
      "title": "Student Admissions Assistant",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Student Admissions Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Student Admissions Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Student Admissions Assistant Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Number 20161769STD Department Summary Student Admissions Assistants “Ambassadors” serve as the student face of Ohio University Southern by welcoming prospective students and families, supporting recruitment initiatives, and promoting the university throughout the Tri-State region. Through conversations and peer-to-peer engagement, ambassadors help prospective students explore educational opportunities, navigate the enrollment process, and envision themselves as future Bobcats. Student Ambassadors work collaboratively with Admissions, the Office of Student Services, faculty, and campus partners to support recruitment events, campus visits, community outreach, and student engagement activities while fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus environment. Job Profile Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Supports the admissions office by processing applications, assisting prospective students and other guests with inquiries, scheduling and conducting campus tours, and providing general administrative support in the admissions process. Represents and communicates the unique student experience at Ohio University. May participate in daily visits, large special visit programs, special group visits, individual VIP tours, and question-and-answer panels. May staff office front desks to welcome and serve campus guests. May conduct out-bound calls to prospective and admitted students family members. May assist with managing inboud emails. Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. The role is entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Communicates externally with prospective students, family members, and other influencers in the college decision making process. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University during the current semester or immediate previous semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Working Condition/Physical Demands: This role requires ability to provide walking tours of campus and escorts guests to various locations across campus, stand for extended periods of time to direct visitors and guests, sit at a desk for extended periods with extensive use of a computer. Occasionally, the job may require travel off-campus to attend meetings and programs. Work Schedule/Location: Responsibilities generally occur between the hours of 8 am and 8 pm Monday through Saturday. However, there may be some work required earlier than 8 am or later than 8 pm or on Sundays. Department Admissions Pay Rate Hourly rate based on university student employment pay scale. FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 08/28/2026 Posting End Date 12/01/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Vice President Enrollment Management Work Schedule 10–20 hours per week, depending on recruitment and campus programming needs. Availability to support evening and weekend recruitment and student engagement activities, as needed. Campus Southern (Ironton, Ohio) Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Jesse \"Tyler\" Grubbs Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Student Admissions Assistant Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57967": {
      "title": "Research Instrumentation Technician",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Research Instrumentation Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Research Instrumentation Technician Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application and attach the following required documents when prompted: Resume or CV A detailed cover letter describing your qualifications, previous experience, and the reasons why you are interested in the position for which you are applying. A list of at least three (3) professional references with current and complete contact details, including an email address. Review of application materials will begin immediately. For full consideration, please apply by the posting closing date. To support relocation to the area, the University may offer a relocation bonus to the selected candidate, subject to eligibility and applicable University guidelines. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Research Instrumentation Technician Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application and attach the following required documents when prompted: Resume or CV A detailed cover letter describing your qualifications, previous experience, and the reasons why you are interested in the position for which you are applying. A list of at least three (3) professional references with current and complete contact details, including an email address. Review of application materials will begin immediately. For full consideration, please apply by the posting closing date. To support relocation to the area, the University may offer a relocation bonus to the selected candidate, subject to eligibility and applicable University guidelines. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016558T Job Description Summary Department Summary This position utilizes a variety of technical skills to provide advanced technical support for the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry through designing, machining, and fabricating custom scientific devices and components from faculty concepts, sketches, CAD drawings, or specifications to perform within precise tolerances; installing and modifying specialized equipment to meet the research needs and functions, and goals; maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing scientific instruments, laboratory equipment, and specialized research devices. Operates and maintains the departmental machine shop equipment including lathe, drills, welding, electrical, vacuum, optical, and filtration systems. Supports laboratory utilities, equipment moves, research-space transitions, and safe handling of compressed gases, vacuum systems, water-purification systems, and potentially contaminated equipment. Works independently with faculty, staff, students, University units, contractors, and vendors to develop practical, safe, and cost-effective solutions for research and instructional needs. Promotes safe laboratory and maintenance practices by educating faculty, staff, students, and others on best practices. Recommend policies to improve the lab environment. Maintain PPE supply, MSDS information, eye wash station, first aid station. Position Profile Provides engineering expertise in designing and maintaining University facilities and systems. Ensures high-quality, innovative infrastructure for the University’s growth. Conducts research and development activities related to the design, development, fabrication, modification, installation, and testing of state-of-the art electronics or electronic components. Responsibilities include programmatic administration, coordination and management of projects, budgetary oversight, facilities management, and leadership of programs and services. Functions may include specialized architectural, engineering, site, and construction services; energy engineering; project scheduling, estimating, and management; and specialized research-related engineering. Level Summary Provides professional expertise to the University community. Serves as a resource and guide to others in the department and/or university. Completes operational tasks essential for the daily functioning of the University. Additionally, contributes to larger projects or initiatives that align with department or University goals, often collaborating across teams. Supervisory Responsibilities May assist in mentoring or training new employees. Fiscal Responsibilities No budgetary responsibility. May be responsible for validating transactions. Problem Solving Handles a variety of problems with some independence. Independence of Action Some supervision; able to work independently on routine tasks. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with team members and shares knowledge. Physical Requirements Working Conditions/Physical Demands: Frequent standing, walking, bending, reaching, climbing, and use of hand and power tools; sustained fine-motor and visual work for precision fabrication and repair. Frequent lifting and carrying of tools, cylinders, parts, and equipment; ability to lift up to 50 pounds independently and to use team lifts, carts, hoists, rigging, or contracted movers for heavier loads. Work in machine-shop and laboratory environments with noise, vibration, sharp tools, hot surfaces, compressed gases, vacuum equipment, chemicals, oils, dust, fumes, and potentially contaminated equipment; required use of appropriate PPE and engineering controls. Occasional work at height, in confined equipment spaces, outdoors, or outside normal business hours when necessary to respond to urgent equipment or utility failures. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Bachelor’s degree in a related field and 3-5 years of related professional experience, or equivalent education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in engineering technology, mechanical engineering, electrical engineering, industrial engineering, chemistry, or a related field is preferred. An Associate degree or completed vocational/technical program in machining, mechanical technology, mechatronics, industrial technology, electrical technology, chemical technology, engineering technology, or a closely related field may substitute for the Bachelor’s degree. An Associate degree will be considered equivalent to two years of education and must be accompanied by a minimum of five years of related professional experience. Applicants without a Bachelor’s degree may be considered with a minimum of seven years of related professional experience in place of the degree requirement. Experience in a chemistry, physics, engineering, biomedical, or other research-intensive laboratory environment. Experience maintaining RO/DI/ultrapure-water systems, vacuum pumps, autoclaves, centrifuges, compressed-gas systems, laser-table installations, or comparable research infrastructure. Proficiency with CAD software and experience producing components from CAD drawings. Training or certification in welding/brazing, rigging or powered industrial trucks, chemical hygiene, hazardous-material awareness, lockout/tagout, or related safety areas. Advanced practical knowledge of machining, fabrication, mechanical systems, materials, tolerances, and repair methods. Working knowledge of chemical compatibility, laboratory hazards, contamination control, and safe work practices in research or industrial environments. Department Chemistry and Biochemistry Pay Rate The starting salary range is $24.65 up to $32.67 per hour, dependent on education, skills, and prior experience and is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan including company contributions, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/ . To support relocation to the area, the University may offer a relocation bonus to the selected candidate, subject to eligibility and applicable University guidelines. Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 17NE Pay Range $24.65-$41.03 FLSA Status Non-Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Engineering, Architecture & Plng Job Sub Family R & D Engineering Job Level IC2NE Job Open Date 10/16/2026 Posting End Date 11/01/2026 Planning Unit College of Arts & Sciences Work Schedule Monday through Friday, usually 8:00 am – 5:00 pm Due to the nature of the work, occasional evening and weekend hours may be required to support critical research or instructional activities, perform equipment maintenance, respond to emergencies, or address other operational needs. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 Expected duration of assignment Ongoing Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Joey Pierce, Employment Coordinator, piercej@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
