    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57932": {
      "title": "Associate Bursar",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Associate Bursar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Associate Bursar Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. THIS POSITION IS CURRENTLY ONLY OPEN TO THE BURSAR'S OFFICE EMPLOYEES. Interested individuals should complete an online application and be prepared to upload the following documents at the time of application: 1. Current CV or Resume 2. Cover Letter For full consideration, please apply by close date. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Associate Bursar Applications Accepted From Intradepartment Special Instructions to Applicants THIS POSITION IS CURRENTLY ONLY OPEN TO THE BURSAR’S OFFICE EMPLOYEES . Interested individuals should complete an online application and be prepared to upload the following documents at the time of application: 1. Current CV or Resume 2. Cover Letter For full consideration, please apply by close date. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016553T Job Description Summary Department Summary This position administers Federal Return to Title IV financial aid calculations to ensure compliance with federal rules and guidelines. The position also supervises billing and collections for entities that sponsor student tuition and fees, as well as the processing of excess financial aid refunds and personal payments. In addition, the position assists with developing and implementing office policies and procedures, testing systems, preparing internal and external reports, and creating e-commerce websites. Position Profile Manages one or more accounting functions. Performs accounting functions such as analyzing, monitoring, reconciling, and reporting financial information. Reviews accounts for errors. Prepares reports, financial statements, and processes other requests for internal and external accounting and auditing. Assists external auditors, as required. Reviews accounts to ensure data integrity. Level Summary Responsible for the management of a unit that performs diverse but related tasks. Handles work and budget planning, ensuring efficient allocation of resources to achieve team objectives. Contributes to divisional or departmental operational plans by aligning unit goals with broader institutional strategies. Accountable for meeting short-term objectives and driving continuous improvement. Supervisory Responsibilities Manages a large team or multiple teams. Directly oversees at least 2.0 FTE employees or one or more supervisors. Has authority to hire, transfer, suspend, promote, manage performance, discharge, assign duties, reward, and discipline employees. Fiscal Responsibilities Oversees large budgets, including departmental and program-level budgets. Problem Solving Solves strategic, organizational problems and ensures continuous improvement. Independence of Action High degree of autonomy in decision-making, accountable for large areas. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with executive leadership and external partners to drive organizational goals. Physical Requirements This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Occasionally, the job may require travel to attend meetings and programs. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Master’s degree in Accounting or in a related field, 8 or more years of related professional experience, and 5 or more years of supervisory experience, or equivalent education and experience. Knowledge of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and accounting practices required. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in higher education, particularly in student accounts and/or student financial aid. Demonstrated interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, including public speaking. Demonstrated organizational and time-management skills, including the ability to balance competing priorities and adapt to shifting needs and deadlines. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and stakeholders in a balanced, collegial, and solution-oriented manner to develop practical and effective solutions. Demonstrated ability to analyze and interpret complex data, identify trends and exceptions, reconcile discrepancies, and translate findings into accurate reports and actionable recommendations. Experience using student information or student enterprise systems to manage student accounts, financial aid, billing, payments, refunds, or related business processes, including system testing, issue resolution, and process improvement. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel, including the ability to analyze large datasets, perform reconciliations, identify exceptions, and develop reports. Demonstrated ability to represent the University professionally and respectfully while addressing sensitive or challenging concerns, including the ability to listen carefully, communicate policies clearly, de-escalate difficult interactions, and work toward practical solutions. Knowledge of federal and state tax requirements applicable to nonresident alien students, including tax withholding and information reporting, with the ability to interpret regulatory guidance and apply it accurately to student account processes. Experience interpreting and applying federal student aid regulations, to ensure compliant and accurate student account and financial aid processes. Department Bursar's Office Pay Rate Salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s education and experience in relation to the minimum qualifications for the position, while also considering internal equity. Employees enjoy a generous benefits package https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits . Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 18 Pay Range $58,972.00-$98,125.00 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Finance & Business Job Sub Family Accounting Job Level M3 Job Open Date 10/15/2026 Posting End Date 10/20/2026 Planning Unit Vice President for Finance & Administration Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm, evenings and weekends as required to meet payroll deadlines or other operational needs as they arise. Position is eligible for hybrid work arrangement with a combination of on-site and remote work. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40+ Expected duration of assignment Ongoing Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Kim Trout, troutk@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
