      "title": "Part-Time Instructor, Center for Law, Justice and Culture (POOL POSTING)",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Part-Time Instructor, Center for Law, Justice and Culture (POOL POSTING) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Part-Time Instructor, Center for Law, Justice and Culture (POOL POSTING) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Center for Law, Justice & Culture is establishing a pool of qualified part-time instructors for the 2026–2027 academic year to teach undergraduate courses as instructional needs arise. Part-time instructional assignments may be available based on student enrollment, course demand, faculty coverage needs, and other departmental instructional needs. Applicants selected for the pool may be contacted when a part-time instructional need arises. Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis through 7/31/2027. Please complete the online application and upload the following: Current CV, Letter of interest, List of three professional references, Unofficial transcripts, Official Candidate LSAT Score Report from the Law School Admission Council, selecting “Other” as the document type when uploading the score report. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Part-Time Instructor, Center for Law, Justice and Culture (POOL POSTING) Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants The Center for Law, Justice & Culture is establishing a pool of qualified part-time instructors for the 2026–2027 academic year to teach undergraduate courses as instructional needs arise. Part-time instructional assignments may be available based on student enrollment, course demand, faculty coverage needs, and other departmental instructional needs. Applicants selected for the pool may be contacted when a part-time instructional need arises. Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis through 7/31/2027. Please complete the online application and upload the following: Current CV, Letter of interest, List of three professional references, Unofficial transcripts, Official Candidate LSAT Score Report from the Law School Admission Council, selecting “Other” as the document type when uploading the score report. This position is eligible for the following benefits: sick leave and retirement. Posting Number 20163229F Job Description Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions as student demand dictates in the Center of Law, Justice and Culture at Ohio University. The instructor pool may support courses designed for undergraduate students preparing for the Law School Admission Test ( LSAT ). Such courses build the cognitive endurance, timing, and error-analysis habits necessary to maximize competitive law school admissions scores. Courses may be offered in person or online, depending on need and demand. Minimum Qualifications B.A. and LSAT score 165 or above Preferred Qualifications J.D. and experience teaching LSAT preparation courses or providing LSAT -related instruction to college or university students and LSAT score 170 or above. Department Center for Law, Justice, and Culture Pay Rate Pay is set according to college approved rates. Please visit A&S Summer and Overload Course Policy | Ohio University for more information. Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. User Selection Field Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Posting Close Date 07/31/2027 Employment Type intermittent term Job Category Instructor Months variable month Planning Unit College of Arts & Sciences Work Schedule Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Joey Pierce, Employment Coordinator, piercej@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Other (See Special Instructions to Applicants for Details) Unofficial transcripts Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
