    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57713": {
      "title": "Orientation Leader",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Orientation Leader Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Orientation Leader Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must be full-time undergraduate students in good academic and disciplinary standing at Ohio University. We encourage you to attend one of our 3 Interest Events on October 21, 22, or 23rd. We will email details to all applicants, or you can email us for information at orientation@ohio.edu Orientation Leaders are required to attend all training sessions (spring UC3690 course and summer training) and work all scheduled Orientation program days. Applicants should be prepared to commit to this role as their primary summer obligation due to the time demands of training and program schedules. Follow-up Interviews will be offered in early November based on availability to select applicants. Selected applicants will be invited to participate in an interview process that may include both individual and group interviews. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Orientation Leader Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be full-time undergraduate students in good academic and disciplinary standing at Ohio University. We encourage you to attend one of our 3 Interest Events on October 21, 22, or 23rd. We will email details to all applicants, or you can email us for information at orientation@ohio.edu Orientation Leaders are required to attend all training sessions (spring UC3690 course and summer training) and work all scheduled Orientation program days. Applicants should be prepared to commit to this role as their primary summer obligation due to the time demands of training and program schedules. Follow-up Interviews will be offered in early November based on availability to select applicants. Selected applicants will be invited to participate in an interview process that may include both individual and group interviews. Posting Number 20161774STD Department Summary The Office of New Student and Family Programs supports the transition and success of Ohio University students and their families. The office oversees Bobcat Student Orientation ( BSO ) , which welcomes and prepares new students for academic and community life at OHIO , as well as ongoing engagement opportunities for families throughout the year. This includes Family Weekend events and other initiatives designed to strengthen the connection between students, their supporters, and the university community. Through these programs, the office helps students build a strong foundation for their college experience while fostering a supportive network for families. Job Profile Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Assists with planning and organizing University events, such as speakers, conferences, or campus gatherings. Duties include coordinating logistics, working with vendors, and managing event details to ensure smooth execution. Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. Roles are entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University, Hocking College, another post-secondary education institution, or a secondary school during the current semester, immediate previous semester, or immediate upcoming semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in a student leadership, peer mentor, ambassador, orientation, or similar role. Strong interpersonal, verbal communication, and presentation skills. Experience facilitating group activities, discussions, or programs. Ability to build positive relationships and engage effectively with students from a variety of backgrounds and experiences. Demonstrated teamwork, dependability, professionalism, and adaptability. Familiarity with campus resources, services, traditions, and student life. Ability to represent the University in a welcoming, professional, and enthusiastic manner. Commitment to creating a welcoming and supportive transition experience for new students and their families. Working Condition/Physical Demands: Navigating campus facilities and outdoor areas, including traveling between meeting locations and activity spaces. Remaining at designated meeting locations for extended periods of time to welcome, orient, and engage participants. Facilitating team-building activities and other interactive programming in a variety of indoor and outdoor settings. Presenting and speaking clearly to groups, including from the front of a classroom or other instructional space. Maintaining active engagement with students through conversation, instruction, demonstrations, and group activities. Working in varying environmental conditions, including indoor and outdoor settings, as required by program activities. Department Dean of Students Pay Rate $3,700 Stipend, Housing and Meal Plan included for time of employment. FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 09/21/2026 Posting End Date 10/25/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Vice President for Student Life Work Schedule Spring Semester: Newly hired Orientation Leaders are required to enroll in and attend UC 3690: The Art of Leading Orientation (to be posted). Summer Training: Orientation Leaders must participate in mandatory training from May 12–26, 2027 . Summer Orientation Programs: Orientation Leaders work all program days on a scheduled rotation, with shifts typically lasting 8–10 hours per day . Work includes mornings, afternoons, and some evening commitments. Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. orientation@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Student Event Coordinator Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What stands out to you about your Orientation experience at OHIO? (Open Ended Question) What interests you about being an Orientation Leader? (Open Ended Question) What motivates you during busy or difficult seasons? (Open Ended Question) What impact do you tend to have on the morale of the people around you? (Open Ended Question) Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57939": {
      "title": "CUSTODIAL WORKER 1",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | CUSTODIAL WORKER 1 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC CUSTODIAL WORKER 1 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open to the public. However, current Ohio University AFSCME 1699 bargaining unit employees will be given first consideration. OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYEES MUST INCLUDE THEIR OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYMENT HISTORY AND ANY RELEVANT VERIFIABLE EXPERIENCE TO SHOW THEY MEET MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR THIS CLASSIFICATION. IF YOUR APPLICATION IS INCOMPLETE YOU WILL BE SCREENED OUT. IF YOU NEED YOUR OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYMENT HISTORY OR NEED ASSISTANCE COMPLETING THE APPLICATION, PLEASE CONTACT UNIVERSITY HUMAN RESOURCES FOR ASSISTANCE. • In an effort to make the process of awarding bid upon positions more efficient, the successful candidate must indicate at the time of offer whether they accept or decline the position • Candidates may contact management during the posting period to ask questions regarding the expectations of the position This is a 9-month (Part-time) Academic Term position. • All positions are subject to seasonal layoff during the summer break, spring break, and winter breaks in accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement and the Ohio Revised Code, due to lack of work during those periods between or outside of academic terms, with reasonable assurance to return to work. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title CUSTODIAL WORKER 1 Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the public , University Wide, AFSCME 1699 Bargaining Unit Wide, AFSCME 1699 Intradepartmental , AFSCME 1699 In-segment Special Instructions to Applicants This position is open to the public. However, current Ohio University AFSCME 1699 bargaining unit employees will be given first consideration. OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYEES MUST INCLUDE THEIR OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYMENT HISTORY AND ANY RELEVANT VERIFIABLE EXPERIENCE TO SHOW THEY MEET MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR THIS CLASSIFICATION . IF YOUR APPLICATION IS INCOMPLETE YOU WILL BE SCREENED OUT . IF YOU NEED YOUR OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYMENT HISTORY OR NEED ASSISTANCE COMPLETING THE APPLICATION , PLEASE CONTACT UNIVERSITY HUMAN RESOURCES FOR ASSISTANCE . • In an effort to make the process of awarding bid upon positions more efficient, the successful candidate must indicate at the time of offer whether they accept or decline the position • Candidates may contact management during the posting period to ask questions regarding the expectations of the position This is a 9-month (Part-time) Academic Term position. • All positions are subject to seasonal layoff during the summer break, spring break, and winter breaks in accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement and the Ohio Revised Code, due to lack of work during those periods between or outside of academic terms, with reasonable assurance to return to work. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 20167079S Job Description Under general direction of a lead worker or supervision by departmental administrator or Building Services Manager, performs duties to provide care, cleaning & maintenance of building, furniture & fixtures. Adheres to all OSHA , CDC and/or Ohio University required safety guidelines; Sweeps, mops, strips, waxes, polishes and renews floor surfaces; Cleans and shampoos rugs and carpets; Washes walls; cleans, dusts and waxes furniture and fixtures following either Level 1 or Level 2 clean/sanitize/disinfect guidelines as directed***; Cleans glass and mirrors; Cleans and empties trash receptacles; May remove and hang drapes; Removes snow and ice from walkways and entrance areas; Reports need for equipment repair; Reports evidence of fire, illegal entry and theft of property; Checks in supplies; stocks supply areas; May assist in washing and sanitizing dishes, glassware, utensils, pots & pans; Cleans and sanitizes bathroom fixtures & drinking fountains; Operates dish machine/pot washer to clean and sanitize dishes, glasses, pans, etc. Performs other related duties as required. ***Applies to Facilities Management and Safety Staff. Minimum Qualifications Knowledge of methods, materials and equipment used in sanitation and safety areas of dining, residential, academic and administrative units; Ability to carry out instructions in written, oral, and pictorial form; Ability to work independently or with others; Willingness to foster a welcoming and respectful workforce and community Ability to read and write common vocabulary in sentence structure; Ability to add, subtract, multiply and divide whole numbers, calculate fractions, decimals and percentages; Ability to apply principles to solve practical problems; Ability to demonstrate dexterity and skill in use of craft-associated hand and/or power tools and equipment; Ability to mix cleaning compounds and follow safety procedures; Ability to lift up to 50 pounds; Ability to effectively use a 15 foot ladder; An established pattern of good work habits and performance with good interpersonal skills. Training & Experience: May require valid driver’s license; Completion of a test may be required. Working Conditions & Physical Requirements: May climb ladders; May be exposed to extreme temperatures; May be exposed to dirt, grease, odors, cramped conditions, extreme hot or cold temperatures, heights, and electrical hazards; May be exposed to dangerous machinery During Level 2 working conditions will be required to wear designated PPE up to and including full body suit, appropriate mask, etc. * *Applies to Facilities Management and Safety Staff. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of custodial safety practices** Skill in operation of cleaning equipment** (electric scrubbers, buffers & vacuum cleaners) Knowledge of all applicable OSHA and/or Ohio University safety guidelines and procedures** **Developed after employment. Working Conditions/Physical Demands Department Culinary Services Pay Rate AFSCME Pay Range | 02 | $15.64– $21.71 Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Job Open Date 10/15/2026 Posting Close Date October 22, 2026 Job Category Classified AFSCME 1699 Bargaining Unit appointment Months Planning Unit Vice President for Student Life Work Schedule Varied Days/Varied Work Hours Part Time and Academic Term position Assigned to Culinary Services Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 30 Expected duration of assignment Permanent Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Jessie Brammer, jessie.brammer@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Job Information Employment Type part-time regular Job Family/Subfamily Career Track & Level Pay Grade AFSCME|02| Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned about this posting. www. ohiouniversityjobs.com www.higheredjobs.com www.ohiomeansjobs.com The Athens Messenger The Chronicle of Higher Education Ohio University employee OHIO Jobs Line (phone) Employment Agency Posted Announcement Professional association Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, etc) OTHER * Please select an option that best represents your current status: I am a current Ohio University employee and NOT currently serving a probationary period. I am a current Ohio University employee, and I am serving in either an initial or a promotional probationary period. I am a current Ohio University Student employee. I am not an employee of Ohio University. * Are you a current Ohio University AFSCME 1699 employee? yes no * Are you a current Ohio University AFSCME 1699 employee working in Culinary Services? yes no Were you referred by an existing Ohio University employee? Please list their name and the date of referral. (Open Ended Question) Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
