    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57941": {
      "title": "ENERGY PLANT OPERATING ENGINEER",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | ENERGY PLANT OPERATING ENGINEER Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC ENERGY PLANT OPERATING ENGINEER Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open to the public. However, current Ohio University AFSCME 1699 bargaining unit employees will be given first consideration. REQUIRED: Stationary Steam Engineers License as per Section 4104.19 of the Revised Code and all requirements of the Ohio Department of Commerce. CURRENT OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYEES MUST INCLUDE THEIR OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYMENT HISTORY AND ANY RELEVANT VERIFIABLE EXPERIENCE TO SHOW THEY MEET THE MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR THIS CLASSIFICATION. IF YOUR APPLICATION IS INCOMPLETE, YOU WILL BE SCREENED OUT. IF YOU NEED YOUR OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYMENT HISTORY OR NEED ASSISTANCE COMPLETING THE APPLICATION, PLEASE CONTACT UNIVERSITY HUMAN RESOURCES FOR ASSISTANCE. In an effort to make the process of warding bid upon positions more efficient, the successful candidate must indicate at the time of offer whether they accept or decline the position. Candidates may contact management during the posting period to ask questions regarding the expectations of the position. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title ENERGY PLANT OPERATING ENGINEER Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the public , University Wide, AFSCME 1699 Bargaining Unit Wide, AFSCME 1699 Intradepartmental , AFSCME 1699 In-segment Special Instructions to Applicants This position is open to the public. However, current Ohio University AFSCME 1699 bargaining unit employees will be given first consideration. REQUIRED : Stationary Steam Engineers License as per Section 4104.19 of the Revised Code and all requirements of the Ohio Department of Commerce. CURRENT OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYEES MUST INCLUDE THEIR OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYMENT HISTORY AND ANY RELEVANT VERIFIABLE EXPERIENCE TO SHOW THEY MEET THE MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR THIS CLASSIFICATION . IF YOUR APPLICATION IS INCOMPLETE , YOU WILL BE SCREENED OUT . IF YOU NEED YOUR OHIO UNIVERSITY EMPLOYMENT HISTORY OR NEED ASSISTANCE COMPLETING THE APPLICATION , PLEASE CONTACT UNIVERSITY HUMAN RESOURCES FOR ASSISTANCE . In an effort to make the process of warding bid upon positions more efficient, the successful candidate must indicate at the time of offer whether they accept or decline the position. Candidates may contact management during the posting period to ask questions regarding the expectations of the position. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 20167081S Job Description Under general supervision from Energy Plant Management, or other high level supervisor; has responsibility for operation of all Energy Plant Facilities (heating plant, chilled water plant, and water treatment plant) associated with the production and distribution of steam, chilled water, and hot water to the entire campus in appropriate quantities, pressure, and temperature. Uses extensive knowledge of systems and application of sound judgment to safely respond to all operating to all operating scenarios, including emergencies. Modulates boilers, chillers and all other plant sub systems, via the use of manual and automated system controls. Provides advise, guidance, training, and back up for the like classifications on the same shift and serves as lead worker (e.g. provides work direction & training) to other bargain unit employees on an assigned shift. Responsible to operate all equipment in a safe, efficient, and environmentally compliant manner. Responsible for plant security and for the safety of all operating personnel assigned while on duty. This work is performed on a 24 hour rotating shift basis. •Adheres to all OSHA and/or Ohio University required safety guidelines. Identifies safety and fire hazards and equipment needing repair throughout the area. Responsible for maintaining a safe work environment for the safety of self and fellow workers. •Serves as lead worker (e.g. provides work direction and training of others) over other workers at Energy Plant on an assigned shift as related to the installation, repair, maintenance, and operation of high pressure boilers (exceeding 15 pounds per square inch), furnaces and auxiliary equipment (i.e. stokers, turbines, blowers, flow meters, pumps, generators, fans, and related equipment) and chillers (electric powered and steam powered), chilled water pumps, and other related chilled water system equipment; and water treatment plant equipment, controls, and other related appurtenances. Responsible to learn new systems as they are introduced to the plant and to assist in the training of personnel in the use of such systems. •Periodically monitors and inspects all areas of responsibility throughout the plant(s) observing conditions of machinery making adjustments as necessary to be certain that all equipment is operating as reliably and efficiently as possible. Such tasks include but are not limited to reading gauges, monitoring power consumption; operating generators, pumps, chillers, and other related equipment. Reports any problems or unusual conditions to plant management. •Oversees the operation of the water treatment plant, assuring that a continuous flow of properly treated water is being supplies. Double checks as necessary laboratory tests and/or chemical analyses and records to assure that makeup water, boiler water, feed water, and campus condensate are all within proper tolerances. •Monitors various environmental parameters to assure compliance with all environmental regulations. Takes appropriate action to eliminate violations within his/her control. •Serves as lead safety officer in the Energy Plant including training other staff in safe work practices. Attends safety training as required. •Operates coal conveyor system and cleans plant and equipment in the absence of other employees. •May be exposed to dirt, dust, fumes, and noise; may be exposed to steam, hot water, and high temperatures. •Performs other related duties as required. Minimum Qualifications •Stationary Steam Engineers License as per Section 4104.19 of the Revised Code and all requirements of the Ohio Department of Commerce. • Possess knowledge of boiler plant operations, baghouse, chilled water plant operations, and water treatment processes associate with plant operations. •Possess knowledge of stationary engineering •Possess skill in operating energy plant equipment •Ability to recognize unusual or threatening conditions and take appropriate emergency action •Ability to understand powerhouse procedures •Ability to carry out instructions in writing, orally, and in pictorial form. •Ability to work independently and with others. •Willingness to foster a welcoming and respectful workforce and community •Ability to demonstrate dexterity and skill in use of craft-associated hand and/or power tools and equipment. •Ability to read & write common vocabulary in sentence structure •Ability to add, subtract, multiply and divide whole numbers, calculate fractions, decimals & percentages. •Ability to apply principles to solve practical problems •Knowledge of all applicable OSHA and/or Ohio University safety guidelines and procedures. •Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. •Successful completion of a written test or practical exam may be required. • An established pattern of good work habits and performance with good interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications •Knowledge of employee mentoring* training* and development* (*Developed after employment) Working Conditions/Physical Demands Department Heating Plant Pay Rate AFSCME |10|$28.28 – $31.82 hourly rate Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Job Open Date 10/15/2026 Posting Close Date November 1, 2026 Job Category Classified AFSCME 1699 Bargaining Unit appointment Months Planning Unit Vice President for Finance & Administration Work Schedule PN100645 Work Days: To be assigned Work Hours: To be assigned Days Off: To be assigned Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 hours per week Expected duration of assignment Permanent Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Eric Burnem, eburnem@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Job Information Employment Type full-time regular Job Family/Subfamily Career Track & Level Pay Grade AFSCME|10| Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned about this posting. www.ohiouniversityjobs.com www.higheredjobs.com www.ohiomeansjobs.com The Athens Messenger The Chronicle of Higher Education Ohio University employee OHIO Jobs Line (phone) Employment Agency Posted Announcement Professional Association Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, etc) OTHER * Please select an option that best represents your current status: I am a current Ohio University employee and NOT currently serving a probationary period. I am a current Ohio University employee, and I am serving in either an initial or a promotional probationary period. I am a current Ohio University Student employee. I am not an employee of Ohio University. * Are you a current Ohio University AFSCME 1699 employee working in the Heating Plant? YES NO * Are you a current Ohio University AFSCME 1699 employee? yes no * Do you currently hold a valid Stationary Steam Engineers License as per Section 4104.19 of the Revised Code? yes no will have at the time of employment Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56116": {
      "title": "Theater Instructors (POOL POSTING)",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Theater Instructors (POOL POSTING) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Theater Instructors (POOL POSTING) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting. Please complete the online application and attach the following documents: Current resume/Curriculum Vitae. Cover letter detailing your interest in this teaching opportunity and/or your teaching philosophy. List of three professional references which includes current contact information. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue as needs arise throughout the year. Please apply by February 16, 2027. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Theater Instructors (POOL POSTING) Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting. Please complete the online application and attach the following documents: Current resume/Curriculum Vitae. Cover letter detailing your interest in this teaching opportunity and/or your teaching philosophy. List of three professional references which includes current contact information. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue as needs arise throughout the year. Please apply by February 16, 2027. This position is eligible for the following benefits: sick leave and retirement. Posting Number 20163070F Job Description This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27 in Theater. We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Theater. Minimum Qualifications A Master’s Degree in Theater (or related field), by the start date of appointment, or the equivalence of through a combination of education and experience in accordance with Ohio University policy 18.001. Preferred Qualifications Department School of Theater Pay Rate Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. User Selection Field Job Open Date 02/19/2026 Posting Close Date Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027. Employment Type Temporary (for group 3 ONLY) Job Category Instructor Months 3 month Planning Unit College of Fine Arts Work Schedule Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Merri Biechler, biechler@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned about this posting. www.ohiouniversityjobs.com www.higheredjobs.com www.ohiomeansjobs.com Ohio University employee OHIO Jobs Line (phone) Twitter Search Firm Professional association OTHER, please indicate: Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
