      "title": "Grounds Specialist-Golf &amp; Tennis Center",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Grounds Specialist-Golf &amp; Tennis Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Grounds Specialist-Golf & Tennis Center Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application and be prepared to upload the following required documents: 1. Resume/CV 2. Cover Letter Questions should be directed to Zach Weeks, Golf Course Superintendent, WeeksZ@ohio.edu Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Grounds Specialist-Golf & Tennis Center Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application and be prepared to upload the following required documents: 1. Resume/CV 2. Cover Letter Questions should be directed to Zach Weeks, Golf Course Superintendent, WeeksZ@ohio.edu Posting Number 20161786STD Department Summary To assist with all aspects of maintenance operations at the Golf and Tennis Center. The role of the Grounds Specialist is to assume responsibilities including, but not limited to, assisting with golf course general maintenance, preventative maintenance, corrective maintenance, and other duties assigned throughout the facilities. Experience and training will include but is not limited to: Assist in day-to-day maintenance (mowing of all surfaces, course set-up, raking bunkers, Pin locations, etc.) General turfgrass management and cultivation on all surfaces. Work with Golf Course Superintendent to identify equipment and facility problems. Work in close relationship with Grounds Supervisors to ensure efficient and proper operation of the facility and equipment. Assist with seasonal course renovations and recovery programs. Perform routine cleaning, inspection, and basic preventive maintenance of equipment. Support other Golf and Tennis Center activities as directed by the Golf Course Superintendent and Assistant Director, Golf & Tennis Center. Maintain organization and cleanliness of golf course maintenance and shop. Participate in professional development and training events. Job Profile Performs a variety of tasks, which may include general facilities maintenance, equipment cleaning and maintenance, performing manual labor, cleaning and preparing rooms for use, landscaping/grounds work, painting, and assisting with campus/facility beautification efforts. Position may operate hand equipment (push mowers, weed eaters, edgers, leaf blowers, etc.) Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. Roles are entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University, Hocking College, another post-secondary education institution, or a secondary school during the current semester, immediate previous semester, or immediate upcoming semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Preferred Qualifications Positive attitude, willingness to learn, and desire to provide outstanding customer service. CPR , First Aid certification Required Experience working in golf course maintenance. Basic skill and confidence in operating movable golf course maintenance equipment. Basic mechanical aptitude and familiarity with small hand or power tools. Summer availability. Working Condition/Physical Demands: Early Starts: Shifts typically begin around 6:00 AM to 8:00 AM to finish high-priority tasks like mowing greens and raking bunkers before golfers arrive. All-Weather Work: Crews work outside through high heat, humidity, rain, and cold morning dew. Heavy Lifting: Workers regularly lift 20-50lbs (Such as sand, and bagged fertilizer) and operate vibrating or heavy machinery for extended periods of time. Repetitive Work: Daily routines involve bending, standing, lifting, walking, and sitting on equipment. Department Well-Being Pay Rate $12.85 / hour FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 10/26/2026 Posting End Date 11/13/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Vice President for Student Life Work Schedule Seasonal Employment: March through November with majority of work taking place between April and the middle of October. Some shifts may be available during winter closure depending on project needs. We will work with you and your academic classes to make your schedule. Willingness to work on occasional weekends, early mornings, or adjusted schedules based on weather, training, and operational requirements. Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Zach Weeks, WeeksZ@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Student Facilities Worker Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
