    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/58009": {
      "title": "Chief of Staff to the VP Finance and Administration",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Chief of Staff to the VP Finance and Administration Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Chief of Staff to the VP Finance and Administration Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application and attach the required documents. Required documents include a detailed cover letter, current resume, and a list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. For full consideration, please submit your materials by position closing date. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Chief of Staff to the VP Finance and Administration Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application and attach the required documents. Required documents include a detailed cover letter, current resume, and a list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. For full consideration, please submit your materials by position closing date. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016563T Job Description Summary Department Summary This position is a trusted advisor and strategic partner, providing guidance on complex divisional issues while ensuring the Finance and Administration division operates efficiently and in compliance with laws, regulations, and university policies. This role requires expertise in data analysis and financial management to support decision-making and advance strategic initiatives. Acting as the eyes and ears for the Vice President, the position oversees critical projects, fosters collaboration, and manages sensitive information with the highest level of discretion. A wide degree of creativity and latitude is expected. Primary Accountabilities: Strategic Support and Planning: Serve as a trusted advisor to the Vice President for Finance and Administration, providing insights and recommendations on sensitive and complex matters. Support the development and execution of the Finance and Administration division’s strategic goals and initiatives. Prepare reports, presentations, and strategic briefs for internal and external stakeholders. Stay informed on federal, state, and local laws, regulations, and university policies, ensuring the Finance and Administration division’s practices and initiatives remain compliant, and initiate policy edits or updates as necessary to maintain alignment with legal and institutional requirements. Identify risks, opportunities, and areas for improvement across the Finance and Administration division. Budget and Data Management: Develop, manage, and forecast the Finance and Administration division’s budget, prepare detailed financial analyses and identify cost-saving opportunities. Prepare detailed budget reports, projections, and financial analyses to support short- and long-term planning. Collaborate with university finance teams to ensure timely submission of budget requests and compliance with financial regulations. Coordinate strategic procurement initiatives and cross-functional evaluation processes in collaboration with appropriate university stakeholders. Utilize data systems to analyze workforce and financial data, generate reports, and provide actionable insights to support strategic decision-making. Ensure compliance with governance policies while optimizing system functionalities. Project Management: Plan, execute, and oversee high-priority Finance and Administration division projects, ensuring they are delivered on time, within scope, and within budget. Develop and maintain project charters, timelines, and management plans. Coordinate cross-functional teams and manage stakeholder communication to ensure project alignment with strategic objectives. Provide leadership in process improvement initiatives to streamline workflows and enhance service delivery. Communication and Relationship Building: Coordinate executive priorities, facilitate leadership engagement, and ensure appropriate follow-up on strategic initiatives and decisions. Act as a liaison between the VP and university leadership, ensuring effective communication and follow-up on key initiatives. Build and maintain relationships with internal and external stakeholders, vendors, and government agencies, representing the Finance and Administration division in various forums. Organize and lead leadership meetings, including setting agendas, preparing materials, and documenting outcomes. Prepare reports and presentations for the VP, ensuring professionalism and confidentiality. Position Profile Manages a variety of highly complex administration processes, such as development and implementation of strategic plans, continuous improvement projects, and stakeholder engagement. May serve on institution-wide committees on behalf of leadership requiring detailed content knowledge and expertise. Utilizes independent judgment and discretion to formulate and manage operational and strategic planning processes. Provides input on financial and strategic viability for initiatives. Ensures effective management of institutional operations through strategic coordination of critical resources. Serves on various department, division, and/or University committees. Level Summary Leads significant programs or functions with a high level of strategic importance. Works as a technical leader to address highly challenging processes with broad and significant implications for the University. Collaborates closely with senior management to deliver impactful business results and long-term strategies. Supervisory Responsibilities Provides subject matter expertise to internal and external stakeholders. May have a limited number of direct reports. Fiscal Responsibilities May manage budget in work area or multiple project budgets. Problem Solving Resolves highly complex problems, often with no clear precedent. Independence of Action Self-directed with minimal supervision and high decision-making autonomy. Communication and Collaboration Leads major collaborations and represents the University at higher levels. Physical Requirements This position is primarily office-based and requires extensive use of computers and other standard office equipment. Duties involve prolonged periods of sitting, frequent communication with internal and external stakeholders, and participation in meetings. The position requires the ability to manage competing priorities, respond to time-sensitive matters, and exercise discretion when handling confidential information. Occasional travel and work outside normal business hours may be required to support university operations, meetings, and special initiatives. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Bachelor’s degree in a related field and 10 or more years of related professional experience, or equivalent education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in business administration, public administration, higher education administration, finance, or a related field. Experience working in higher education, government, or another large, complex organization. Demonstrated experience supporting executive leadership in strategic planning, organizational initiatives, and complex decision-making. Experience with financial analysis, budget development, forecasting, and resource allocation. Demonstrated success managing complex projects and leading cross-functional initiatives involving multiple stakeholders. Strong analytical, communication, and relationship-building skills, including experience preparing executive-level reports, presentations, and recommendations. Knowledge of organizational governance, policy development, and regulatory compliance. Department VP For Finance and Administration Pay Rate Competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Employees enjoy a generous benefits package https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 20 Pay Range $80,593.00-$138,208.00 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Administrative Management Job Sub Family Administrative Strategy Job Level IC5 Job Open Date 10/27/2026 Posting End Date 11/17/2026 Planning Unit Vice President for Finance & Administration Work Schedule Typical work expectations are Monday – Friday, 8:00 – 5:00; however, candidates must be willing to work evenings and/or weekends if necessary. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 + Expected duration of assignment on-going Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Vickie Wortman, wortmanv@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
