    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/58012": {
      "title": "Regional Recruitment Manager (Southwest Ohio)",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Regional Recruitment Manager (Southwest Ohio) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Regional Recruitment Manager (Southwest Ohio) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is being posted in conjunction with: https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57827 Only one position will be filled. The university is posting both positions to ensure a sufficient applicant pool to fill this need. The hiring department will first consider applicants from the higher-level position. If the applicant pool does not yield a successful candidate, the applicant pool from the lower-level position will then be evaluated. If the lower-level posting yields the successful candidate, the hiring department intends to develop the candidate in preparation for the higher-level position. Applicants are encouraged to apply for either or both positions based upon their qualifications and interests. To apply, after reviewing the position profile below, please submit the online application, a current resume and cover letter addressing your professional interest in this role. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For priority consideration, apply by October 26, 2026. For full consideration apply by November 9, 2026. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Regional Recruitment Manager (Southwest Ohio) Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants This position is being posted in conjunction with: https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57827 Only one position will be filled. The university is posting both positions to ensure a sufficient applicant pool to fill this need. The hiring department will first consider applicants from the higher-level position. If the applicant pool does not yield a successful candidate, the applicant pool from the lower-level position will then be evaluated. If the lower-level posting yields the successful candidate, the hiring department intends to develop the candidate in preparation for the higher-level position. Applicants are encouraged to apply for either or both positions based upon their qualifications and interests. To apply, after reviewing the position profile below, please submit the online application, a current resume and cover letter addressing your professional interest in this role. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For priority consideration, apply by October 26, 2026. For full consideration apply by November 9, 2026. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016543T Job Description Summary Department Summary Ohio University is seeking a relationship driven professional to serve as a Regional Recruitment Manager ( RRM ), supporting undergraduate recruitment and enrollment goals in Southwest Ohio. This position will guide prospective students and families through the admissions process, applying strong knowledge of academic programs, policies, and student services to support informed decision making. Through strategic outreach, personalized engagement, and thoughtful territory management, the RRM plays an important role in shaping enrollment outcomes and strengthening OHIO’s presence in the region. Based in the Cincinnati area, the RRM will plan and execute recruitment activities for assigned territories, including travel, outreach, and engagement initiatives. The position will represent Ohio University at high impact events, build and maintain relationships with students, families, school counselors, and community partners, and communicate OHIO’s strengths through clear, student centered messaging. In addition to evaluating applications and contributing to admission decisions, the position will help ensure a consistent and student focused review process. This role leverages recruitment and enrollment data to refine outreach strategies, contributes to team initiatives, and collaborates closely with colleagues across Undergraduate Admissions. The Regional Recruitment Manager position is ideal for a motivated, people centered professional who thrives in a fast paced environment, enjoys balancing independent work with collaboration, and is committed to supporting students as they navigate their educational pathways. Position Profile Recruits, evaluates, and participates in the selection of candidates for University admission. Coordinates with all internal departments, external organizations, and individuals involved in the admissions process. Advises applicants and parents about educational planning. Ensures the effective and compliant processing of student applications. Level Summary Manages and resolves complex and ambiguous issues. Works on both strategic and operational challenges, addressing problems that require advanced knowledge and experience. Often takes on leadership roles in projects or initiatives. Supervisory Responsibilities Provides mentorship and guidance to team. Infrequently has a limited number of direct reports. Fiscal Responsibilities May have budgetary responsibility for small-scale projects or initiatives. Problem Solving Solves complex problems, often with limited guidance. Independence of Action Works independently; seeks guidance for unusual situations. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with team members and external departments. May represent the team in meetings with internal and external stakeholders. Physical Requirements This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Significant travel, including some overnights and weekends, within assigned territory is required. Travel to Ohio University for training, on-campus events, and collaboration with admissions staff and university colleagues is also expected. Must be able to travel independently. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Bachelor’s degree in a related field and 5 or more years of related professional experience, or equivalent education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Candidates with a master’s degree are strongly preferred. Preference given to candidates living in the Cincinnati, Ohio metro area. Previous experience in college admissions, academic advising in higher education, college student personnel, or counseling or teaching in secondary schools; demonstrated interpersonal and written communication and public speaking skills. Demonstrated organizational and time management skills. Ability to work collaboratively. Data analysis experience. The incumbent is able to represent the University in a professional and positive manner and abide by the National Association for College Admission Counseling’s Guide to Ethical Practice in College Admission. Ability to travel independently including overnight and internationally. Ability to pass background checks, university judiciary review, and regular driving history audits. Department Admissions Pay Rate The Regional Recruitment Manager is mapped to Pay Grade CA&P 16 at OHIO , with a target hiring range of $44,592 – $59,085. The exact starting salary for the selected candidate will be negotiable, commensurate with education and experience, and competitive in the field within the context of similarly situated positions at public universities nationally. Pay is commensurate with experience and credentials and is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan including company contributions, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/ . Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 16 Pay Range $44,592.00-$74,196.00 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Enrollment Services Job Sub Family University Admissions & Recruitment Job Level IC3 Job Open Date 10/12/2026 Posting End Date 11/09/2026 Planning Unit Vice President Enrollment Management Work Schedule Monday – Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. EST . Some evenings and weekend work may be required (generally with advance notice). This is a remote position, based in assigned territory. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 Expected duration of assignment Ongoing Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Jennifer Dillie, dillie@ohio.edu, 740.593.4102 Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your level of education achieved: No degree Associate's Degree Bachelor's Degree conferred by start date Master's Degree Ph.D. or other terminal degree * Please indicate your level of related work experience. None Less than one year At least one year but less than three years At least three years but less than five Five or more years Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/58014": {
      "title": "Pre-Award Manager - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Pre-Award Manager - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Pre-Award Manager - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application and attach the required documents. Required documents include a detailed cover letter, current resume, and a list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by 11:59 p.m. on November 15, 2026. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Pre-Award Manager - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application and attach the required documents. Required documents include a detailed cover letter, current resume, and a list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by 11:59 p.m. on November 15, 2026. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016546T Job Description Summary Department Summary About the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine: Mission: We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio. Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community commits itself to: providing a clinically integrated, learning-centered, osteopathic medical education continuum for students, interns, residents and primary care associates; embracing public service; and improving the health and well-being of underserved populations. Vision: A healthier Ohio, empowered by compassionate osteopathic physicians. With our graduates and partners, we advance care and knowledge to improve the health of our communities. Our culture is built upon resiliency, courage and compassion. Our physicians humanize each patient encounter, bridging the gap between therapeutics, medical technologies, health systems, care delivery and disparity. Essential Values: These fundamental principles form the foundation of the culture at our college: wholeness and balance within each person; integrity; community of mutual respect; acceptance of others; pursuit of excellence; a climate of scholarship; and commitment to service, generosity and compassion. Our Campuses: https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses Why Choose Ohio University? https://www.ohio.edu/hr/jobs/working-ohio https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits About the Office of Research and Grants Department Summary: The Pre-Award Manager provides comprehensive proposal development and submission support to faculty, researchers, and administrative staff seeking external funding. This position serves as a primary resource throughout the pre-award lifecycle, assisting with the interpretation of sponsor guidelines and application requirements; development of proposal submission plans and timelines; preparation of proposal checklists; development of complex budgets and budget justifications; and coordination of proposal components from internal and external collaborators. The Pre-Award Manager acts as a liaison among principal investigators, institutional offices, and collaborating organizations to facilitate proposal submission activities, obtain and manage subaward documentation, and ensure proposal requirements are met. This position is responsible for developing and assembling proposals in Cayuse and other electronic research administration systems and facilitating proposal uploads to sponsor submission portals. This position works closely with faculty, departmental administrators, research staff, and central university offices to coordinate multiple concurrent proposal submissions while maintaining a high standard of quality, accuracy, and customer service. Working in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment, the Pre-Award Manager must demonstrate exceptional organizational and problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and the ability to independently manage multiple competing priorities. Success in this role requires strong communication and interpersonal skills, a comprehensive understanding of sponsor requirements and grant proposal processes, and the ability to build collaborative relationships with internal and external stakeholders to ensure timely, compliant, and competitive proposal submissions. Position Profile Participates in contract proposals and negotiations. Directs and manages the authorization and transmittal of all proposals to federal, state, and private funding agencies, ensuring compliance with federal, state, and institutional policies. Monitors grants and contracts to ensure expenses are being paid according to contract. Maintains contract renewal schedules. Level Summary Manages and resolves complex and ambiguous issues. Works on both strategic and operational challenges, addressing problems that require advanced knowledge and experience. Often takes on leadership roles in projects or initiatives. Supervisory Responsibilities Provides mentorship and guidance to team. Infrequently has a limited number of direct reports. Fiscal Responsibilities May have budgetary responsibility for small-scale projects or initiatives. Problem Solving Solves complex problems, often with limited guidance. Independence of Action Works independently; seeks guidance for unusual situations. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with team members and external departments. May represent the team in meetings with internal and external stakeholders. Physical Requirements This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Occasionally, the job may require travel to attend meetings and programs. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Bachelor’s degree in a related field and 5 or more years of related professional experience, or equivalent education and experience. Preferred Qualifications 2 – 3 years of pre-award experience Experience assisting with the development of NIH , NSF and ODH grant proposals Strong project management, organizational, and workflow management skills. Ability to manage multiple proposal deadlines, competing priorities, and complex submission portfolios simultaneously. Experience interpreting sponsor guidelines and coordinating grant proposal preparation and submission activities. Experience developing complex budgets and budget justifications for federal, state, foundation, and other sponsored projects. Proficiency with Cayuse, federal grant submission systems (e.g., Grants.gov, ASSIST , Research.gov), sponsor-specific electronic submission platforms, and Microsoft Office applications. Ability to work independently while fostering collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, institutional offices, external partners, and collaborating organizations. Demonstrated ability to coordinate and manage multiple concurrent proposals while maintaining compliance with sponsor and institutional requirements. Knowledge of sponsored programs administration principles, including pre-award regulations, proposal development processes, and sponsor requirements. Commitment to providing high-quality customer service and responsive support to faculty and research personnel. Department HCOM - Research and Grants Pay Rate The approved hiring range for this position is $51,281 to $67,947 . Offers outside of this range require additional approvals. The final offer will be commensurate with the candidate’s education and experience in relation to the minimum qualifications for the position. Pay is accompanied by Ohio University’s generous benefits package, which includes: Free tuition for employees and dependents Comprehensive insurance coverage, including health, prescription, vision, dental, orthodontia, and life insurance An excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution Wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a robust employee assistance program Paid parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more Additional information is available at: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/ Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 17 Pay Range $51,281.00-$85,325.00 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Research Administration Job Sub Family Contracts & Grants Job Level IC3 Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Posting End Date 11/15/2026 Planning Unit Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine Work Schedule Normal working hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. The position requires flexibility to accommodate sponsor deadlines, proposal submission schedules, and other time-sensitive activities. As a result, work outside of normal business hours, including evenings and weekends, may periodically be required. This position is eligible for remote or on-campus work, consistent with university policies and departmental needs. Employees may be required to travel periodically to the Athens campus to participate in meetings, training sessions, strategic planning activities, and other functions necessary to support sponsored programs administration, proposal development, and pre-award research administration activities. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 Expected duration of assignment Ongoing Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Jordyn Boyer, jboyer@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you find this job posting? Indeed LinkedIn Ohio University Jobs Publication/Print Ad Referred by Person Other Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/58025": {
      "title": "Payroll Operations Lead",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Payroll Operations Lead Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Payroll Operations Lead Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please complete and submit the online application and be prepared to attach 3 separate documents: Current resume, Cover Letter, and a list of 3 professional references with current contact information including email addresses. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, please apply by the posting end date. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Payroll Operations Lead Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please complete and submit the online application and be prepared to attach 3 separate documents: Current resume, Cover Letter, and a list of 3 professional references with current contact information including email addresses. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, please apply by the posting end date. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016550T Job Description Summary Department Summary Under the direction of the Director of Payroll, the Payroll Operations Lead oversees end-to-end payroll operations, ensures compliance with federal, state, and local regulations, and partners with HR and finance to resolve complex pay issues. This role drives system enhancements and process improvements, leads special payroll projects (e.g., retroactive adjustments, off-cycle runs), serves as the primary escalation point for policy interpretation, and coaches junior payroll staff to maintain accuracy and timeliness in all payroll activities. Position Profile Responsible for payroll processing activities, including regular and overtime pay processing, employee and employer contributions/withholdings, vacation and sick time accruals, and payroll taxes. Level Summary Regularly serves as a technical leader, expert, or program manager for complex functions or initiatives that require deep subject-matter knowledge. Significantly impacts the department by directly contributing to its performance and success. Supervisory Responsibilities Provides leadership to projects or initiatives. May have a limited number of direct reports. Fiscal Responsibilities May be responsible for budget for projects or initiatives. Problem Solving Leads problem-solving efforts across various challenges. Independence of Action Operates with high autonomy and is trusted to make decisions. Communication and Collaboration Frequently collaborates cross-functionally and represents the team in meetings with internal and external stakeholders. Influences decision-making. Physical Requirements This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Occasionally, the job may require travel to attend meetings and programs. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Bachelor’s degree in a related field and 8 or more years of related professional experience, or equivalent education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Experience serving as a payroll team lead, or senior payroll subject matter expert, including providing technical guidance, training, and support to other payroll professionals. Experience administering payroll in a higher education, public-sector, or similarly complex decentralized organization. Advanced knowledge of federal, state, and local payroll requirements, including wage and hour laws, payroll taxation, garnishments, and applicable reporting requirements in a multistate payroll environment. Experience processing and reconciling complex payroll transactions, researching discrepancies, conducting audits, and implementing process improvements. Experience using enterprise payroll and human resources information systems, such as Oracle, Workday, or PeopleSoft to process payroll, research issues, perform reconciliations, or support reporting. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel, including the ability to analyze large datasets, perform reconciliations, identify exceptions, and develop payroll reports. Experience supporting payroll system implementations, upgrades, testing, or process automation initiatives, including documenting requirements, validating results, or resolving defects. Certified Payroll Professional ( CPP ) designation or equivalent advanced payroll training or certification. Department Payroll Pay Rate Pay range for this position $68,299 – $117,127 and offer will be commensurate with the candidate’s education and experience in relation to the minimum qualifications for the position. Ohio University is proud to offer a generous benefits package which includes full health benefits, paid time off, and educational benefits for employees and their eligible dependents. Additional information is available at https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits . Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 19 Pay Range $68,299 – $117,127 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Finance & Business Job Sub Family Payroll Job Level IC4 Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Posting End Date 11/01/2026 Planning Unit Vice President for Finance & Administration Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm, evenings and weekends as required to meet payroll deadlines or other operational needs as they arise. Position is eligible for hybrid work arrangement with a combination of on-site and remote work. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 + Expected duration of assignment On-going Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Bridget Driggs - driggsb@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
