    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/58018": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant, Communications &amp; Engagement",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Graduate Assistant, Communications &amp; Engagement Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Graduate Assistant, Communications & Engagement Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Applicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. The information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, complete the online application and upload required documents including a cover letter documenting qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae/resume, and a list of at least three professional references including at least one prior or current supervisor. The list of references should include name and current contact information. A job offer is contingent on acceptance into an Ohio University graduate program. This position includes a 1-year contract with possibility of a second year dependent on your graduate program restrictions and needs of the department. Well-Being will provide a stipend, however, a tuition waiver is dependent on approval from your academic department and is not guaranteed. Graduate Assistants will be expected to report for onboarding, training and semester preparation in August. The final date is to be determined. Questions should be directed to: Gina Mace Assistant Director, Marketing and Engagement maceg@ohio.edu Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Graduate Assistant, Communications & Engagement Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, complete the online application and upload required documents including a cover letter documenting qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae/resume, and a list of at least three professional references including at least one prior or current supervisor. The list of references should include name and current contact information. A job offer is contingent on acceptance into an Ohio University graduate program. This position includes a 1-year contract with possibility of a second year dependent on your graduate program restrictions and needs of the department. Well-Being will provide a stipend, however, a tuition waiver is dependent on approval from your academic department and is not guaranteed. Graduate Assistants will be expected to report for onboarding, training and semester preparation in August. The final date is to be determined. Questions should be directed to: Gina Mace Assistant Director, Marketing and Engagement maceg@ohio.edu Posting Number 20161779STD Department Summary This position provides experience in marketing, promotions, communication, digital and social media, and design/layout. This position supervises a student marketing team in the promotion and communication of all programs and facilities housed in Counseling and Psychological Services, Well-Being and Rec including the following: Aquatic Center, Bird Ice Arena, Charles J. Ping Recreation Center, Golf and Tennis Center, Walter Fieldhouse, Well-Being & Fitness, Intramural and Club Sports, Outdoor Pursuits, and WellWorks. In addition, the marketing team works to brand the department as one cohesive unit to include both university and department brand standards, consistency in the output of marketing materials and social media accounts, and a consistent voice for Counseling and Psychological Services, and Well-Being and Rec. Additionally, this position will serve as a contact for University Communications and Marketing, and the Division of Student Life Marketing Team to provide content and information for university communications and social media accounts. The OHIO Well-Being marketing team work closely to enhance department communication and ensure our users and staff receive regular, current communication to share opportunities for students to engage in our programs and facilities while promoting Ohio University’s commitment to Well-Being. The Graduate Assistant for Marketing will be challenged with promoting Well-Being & Recreation to the OHIO population and surrounding Athens community. As a Graduate Assistant, you will collaborate with the student marketing staff and the Director of Operations and Engagement to oversee the department’s Marketing and Communication annual plan and implementation. This position will be tasked with overseeing the day-to-day operations of the marketing department including the oversight of marketing requests, intake, and material distribution, project management and supervision of student staff to develop a cohesive marketing and communication plan for all programs and activities to include digital media materials, direct mail, digital newsletter content, flyers, orientation and community guides, posters, social media content and digital advertisements. This position will need to be driven, creative, and an independent thinker as you will be challenged with promoting to diverse audiences. This position requires collaboration in supporting the promotion and registration of department events and programs while maintaining University marketing standards, brand and values. Direct oversight for the following: Social Media Accounts, RISE Vision (Digital Displays), OHIO CUE Calendar, TDX project management and intake, OHIO Well-Being and Recreation Website, and student staff. Job Profile Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Engages with students and contributes to the growth and development of various aspects of the Ohio University experience, including student engagement, student leadership, student conduct, well-being and recreation, academic success, and campus life. Responsibilities may include supporting student government, developing student fitness and recreation programs, coordinating student events, providing student academic support, and providing administrative support to departments across the University. Level Summary Provides specialized assistance in academic or administrative tasks, leveraging advanced knowledge in a particular subject area. Supports faculty, researchers, or departments in a variety of ways. Supervisory Responsibilities: May supervise undergraduate students. Fiscal Responsibilities: May assist in managing small budgets for research projects or departmental activities. Problem Solving: Handles complex, field-specific problems that require critical thinking and independent analysis. May require guidance for highly specialized or unfamiliar tasks, but able to handle day-to-day challenges independently. Independence of Action: Works independently on assigned tasks but may consult with faculty or staff for major decisions. Communication and Collaboration: Regular communication with faculty, supervisors, and peers. Collaborates with academic and administrative peers, faculty, and staff and participates in meetings or discussions to further research or projects. May interact with students, colleagues, or clients in academic settings. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Must be a graduate student currently enrolled in an Ohio University academic program. Must have strong research, writing, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in marketing, Communication, Public Relations, Advertising, Business or related field preferred Demonstrate the willingness and ability to lead and learn Proficient computer skills as well as strong written and oral communication skills High level of professionalism in dealing with customers, professional staff, and student employees Experience supervising a team or group of staff Creative thinker with strong communication and project management experience Experience with Adobe Creative Suite preferred Comprehensive experience in project management software: Trello, Airtable, Teamwork, etc. Experience in DSE Experience in Drupal or other content management systems Experience in Well-Being & Recreation either as a user or employee Working Condition/Physical Demands: This position is primarily office-based and requires frequent use of computer and standard office equipment. Occasional travel across campus may be necessary to attend meetings and support events and programs. Department Well-Being Business Operations Pay Rate $13,500 Annual Stipend FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 10/08/2026 Posting End Date 11/14/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Vice President for Student Life Work Schedule Graduate Assistants are expected to work a total of 300 hours over the course of the semester. This averages out to approximately 20 hours per week. Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Gina Mace, maceg@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level GRADSTUDENT Job Family Graduate Student Employee Job Sub Family Graduate Assistantship Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
  },
